 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Where to look**\n\n- `src/tessel/app.py:1184-1189`: `Tessel.link_for` raises this error when `url_adapter` is `None`. Outside a request, the adapter comes from `self.build_url_binder(None)`, which can only return one if `SERVER_NAME` is set.\n- `src/tessel/helpers.py:200`: the `link_for` helper delegates to `active_app.link_for`. It needs an active app context, so the job must run inside `app.app_context()`.\n\n**Fix**\n\nSet these in the app config:\n\n```python\napp.config[\"SERVER_NAME\"] = \"example.com\"        # required\napp.config[\"APPLICATION_ROOT\"] = \"/\"             # if mounted under a prefix\napp.config[\"PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME\"] = \"https\"     # default is usually http\n```\n\nRun the job inside `with app.app_context():`. Links built outside a request come out as external, absolute URLs using that host and scheme.",
